    <DataNode elementId="AT2G30490-MONOMER" textLabel="cinnamate 4-hydroxylase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="P92994" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="595" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The cDNA encoding cinnamate-4-hydroxylase (C4H - CYP73A5) was isolated from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; and recombinantly expressed in insect cells, and its function demonstrated. The enzyme is encoded by a single-copy gene and appears to be coordinatedly expressed with other genes coding for enzymes such as phenylalanin-ammonium-lyase (PAL) and cinnamoyl-ligases (4CL) |CITS: [9085571]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G30490-MONOMER" />
